			"Message": "refactor(Output): Reorganize service files into semantic directory structure\n\nRestructure the flattened service directory in the Output element to reflect the logical grouping of CodeEditorLand (CEL) components and external dependencies.\n\nMove previously flat service files (`CELExposeAccessor`, `CELExtensionsScannerService`, `DevLog`, etc.) into their respective namespace folders under `Source/Service/` (e.g., `CEL/Expose/`, `CEL/Null/`, `Tauri/Main/Process/`). The `ApplyPipeline.ts` file is also moved to `Source/Apply/`. All file contents remain unchanged (100% similarity), preserving the PascalCase naming conventions and logical behavior established in recent formatting commits.\n\nThis reorganization improves navigability and aligns the file system with the architectural modularity of the CEL service layer, facilitating future development and maintenance of the bundled artifacts.",
			"SHA": "85e32b1a6abe85a4a29799e4b3b97008daa343a9"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-04T15:09:36Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				397,
				6
			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Fix webview iframe hanging by patching ServiceWorker and event activation\n\nAddress critical UI stalls where extension webviews and sidebar panes remain stuck at the bare chrome (`pre/index.html`).\n\n1. **Webview Shell Patch (Plugin):** Add `PatchWebviewIframeServiceWorker` to the ESBuild pipeline. Under Tauri 2 + WKWebView, the custom `vscode-webview://` protocol rejects ServiceWorker registration, causing the bootstrap script to await a rejected promise and bail with `fatal-error`. This plugin forces `disableServiceWorker = true` and soft-fails strict `parentOrigin` hash checks that fail on custom protocols, ensuring the iframe renders correctly.\n\n2. **Extension Activation Patch (Service):** Enhance `CELExposeAccessor` to short-circuit `IExtensionService.activateByEvent` for `onView:*` events. Since Land's `*` activation pass loads all extensions at boot, waiting for specific view events (which block `WebviewViewPane.activate`) creates a deadlock in Cocoon. Immediate resolution prevents sidebar stalls.\n\nThese changes resolve hangs in extension webviews and sidebar views without forking the upstream workbench bootstrap logic.",
			"SHA": "57b2a1a56c41c5e61dcc2dd421aaf5a555a80d37"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-04T11:29:14Z",
			"File": [
