				"⣿⡏⠀⠀⠀",
				380,
				120
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Output): Reformat build configuration and plugin pipeline for readability\n\nReformat the entire Output element's ESBuild configuration, plugin definitions, exclusion patterns, and polyfill scripts to align with the project's PascalCase naming conventions and readability standards. This change follows the previous minification commits by restoring source formatting without altering logical behavior.\n\nKey modifications:\n- Revert minified variable names in entry points (`Configuration/ESBuild/CodeEditorLand/Editor.js`, `Bundle.js`) and exclusion scripts (`Bootstrap`, `Electron`, `Telemetry`, etc.) to explicit identifiers and expand dense block structures.\n- Refactor plugin definitions (`Configuration/Plugin/Index.js`, `Apply.js`) and transform logic (`Configuration/Plugin/Transform/`) to use multi-line structures and detailed comments explaining the rationale for each excluded path or transform.\n- Expand polyfill implementations (`Configuration/Plugin/Polyfill/`) and service modules (`Configuration/Service/`) to restore whitespace, indentation, and function names.\n- Reformat the Rest plugin (`Configuration/ESBuild/RestPlugin.js`) and output configuration (`Configuration/ESBuild/Output.js`) to align with the project's style guide.\n\nThe logical behavior of the build pipeline remains unchanged; this commit solely addresses source formatting, documentation consistency, and the introduction of new service modules like `CELExposeAccessor`.\n\nRefs #65058a0e1555a69544fbef42ff813a85eaab7f07",
			"SHA": "0de0ae14ad1d9d191f1a82016950854b04954f91"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-04T10:40:16Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⣿⡟⠀⠀",
				369,
				202
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Output): Reformat build configuration and plugin pipeline for readability\n\nReformat the entire Output element's ESBuild configuration, plugin definitions, polyfills, and service modules to align with the project's PascalCase naming conventions and readability standards. This change follows the previous minification commits by restoring source formatting without altering logical behavior.\n\nKey modifications:\n- Rename minified bindings (e.g., `t` → `Prefix`, `e` → `Current`, `o` → `Browser`) and expand dense block structures in `Configuration/ESBuild/CodeEditorLand/Editor.js` and `Bundle.js`.\n- Refactor exclusion patterns (`Configuration/ESBuild/Exclude/` scripts like `Bootstrap`, `ChromiumIPC`, `Electron`, `Network`, `Telemetry`) to include detailed comments explaining the rationale for each excluded path and restore whitespace.\n- Refactor plugin definitions (`Configuration/Plugin/Index.js`, `Apply.js`, `Copy.js`) and transform logic (`Configuration/Plugin/Transform/`) to use explicit variable names and multi-line structures for clarity.\n- Expand polyfill implementations (`Configuration/Polyfill/`) and service modules (`Configuration/Service/TauriMainProcessService.js`, `DevLog.js`) to restore whitespace, indentation, and function names (e.g., `DisableLazyPaint`, `EagerExtensionActivation`).\n- Rename `Configuration/ESBuild/Output.js` from `Source/ESBuild/Output.js` (deleted) and reformat its content.\n- Add source map files (`.js.map`) for all modified configurations to support debugging.\n\nThe logical behavior of the build pipeline remains unchanged; this commit solely addresses source formatting, documentation consistency, and the introduction of the `CELExposeAccessor` service and its supporting TypeScript source in `Source/Service/`.",
			"SHA": "65058a0e1555a69544fbef42ff813a85eaab7f07"
		}
